{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880204",
      "title": "How To Use Template Refs",
      "lectureOrder": 296,
      "videoOrder": 263,
      "sourceHash": "4d788878d866da7a9784693b8e422626930e533d79401ad4e817fc837164b08c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "Let's start with refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 7.64,
          "en": "And now I don't mean refs in the setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.64,
          "end": 10.49,
          "en": "which are our reactive values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.49,
          "end": 15.193,
          "en": "But I mean, refs referring to elements in our template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.39,
          "end": 20.12,
          "en": "Let's say for the LastName, for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.12,
          "end": 22.133,
          "en": "we don't want to use the model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23,
          "end": 26.541,
          "en": "Instead here, I want to use set a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.541,
          "end": 27.708,
          "en": "LastNameInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 31.45,
          "en": "And I want to use the approach you saw a couple of times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.45,
          "end": 34.51,
          "en": "throughout the course, where I read the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.51,
          "end": 38.46,
          "en": "from an input by using this $ ref's variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.46,
          "end": 42.7,
          "en": "inside of some method in our config object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.7,
          "end": 45.5,
          "en": "So let's say we want to do the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.5,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "So we have a button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 52.61,
          "en": "Set Name, where upon a click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.27,
          "end": 56.23,
          "en": "I want to call some setName function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.23,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "and that function should then set the LastName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 62.08,
          "en": "Actually therefore, I will name it setLastName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.365,
          "end": 65.013,
          "en": "and name the function setLastName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "Now, of course, first of all, we created that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 73.513,
          "en": "So we add a new function in the setup method setLastName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 77.42,
          "en": "This function receives no arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.42,
          "end": 81.292,
          "en": "But in here, I now want to set LastName.Value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.292,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "referring to the value prop of my LastName ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "equal to the value stored in this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 92.65,
          "en": "And for this, historically, with the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.65,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "we would have used this $refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 99.03999999999999,
          "en": "and then our ref name here, which is LastNameInput.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 103.15,
          "end": 105.22999999999999,
          "en": "This won't work here though, because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.22999999999999,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "inside of the setup method, you don't have access to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.05,
          "en": "as you're used to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.05,
          "end": 114.17,
          "en": "You won't find $refs thing there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.17,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "Instead, the approach is the other way around you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 122.18,
          "en": "Now you've defined your refs, including your template refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.18,
          "end": 124.67,
          "en": "like this one, in the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.67,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "There is no differentiation between your own refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 131.33,
          "en": "that manage your own data, and refs you want to bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.33,
          "end": 132.873,
          "en": "to some DOM element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 136.94,
          "en": "So here you simply create a new ref LastNameInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 140.3,
          "end": 141.653,
          "en": "by calling ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.38,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "The initial value here is now because initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.36,
          "en": "this is not bound to any element in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.36,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "But now we can simply expose LastNameInput to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 156.4,
          "en": "by returning it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.4,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "Maybe instead of LastName, which we now don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 161.48,
          "en": "in the template anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.48,
          "end": 165.151,
          "en": "We now expose LastNameInput, and also already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.151,
          "end": 168.23,
          "en": "the setLastName function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.23,
          "end": 171.02,
          "en": "So expose this function as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.02,
          "end": 174.023,
          "en": "So now this new ref and this function is exposed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175,
          "end": 179.13,
          "en": "And now LastNameInput is bound to this input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.13,
          "end": 181.38,
          "en": "because we're using the same name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.38,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "And you still assign a ref like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 187.12,
          "en": "just a string with the ref name that you created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.12,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "in your setup function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 192.44,
          "en": "So LastName and put here, once it's exposed to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.44,
          "end": 196.66,
          "en": "like this is then available under that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.66,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "for this special a ref prop, which you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 203.23,
          "en": "on any DOM element of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.23,
          "end": 205.78,
          "en": "And Vue will make the connection behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 211,
          "en": "And with that, we'll be able to go to our setLastName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "function here, and simply get the value from that input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 219.513,
          "en": "by accessing LastNameInput.value.value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.86,
          "end": 224.81,
          "en": "Now this might look strange, this .value.value thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.81,
          "end": 228.1,
          "en": "keep in mind you always get access to the value of a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 228.1,
          "end": 230.02,
          "en": "with .value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.02,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "And the value of this ref will be a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 236.89,
          "en": "at this input element object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.89,
          "end": 240.52,
          "en": "And this object in turn will also have a value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.52,
          "end": 242.24,
          "en": "holding the user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.24,
          "end": 245.26,
          "en": "So the second .value is getting access to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 245.26,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "that value property of the input element object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 252.31,
          "en": "the first .value gets access to the value of our ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.31,
          "end": 254.543,
          "en": "which then is that input element object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.9,
          "end": 257.98,
          "en": "With that we get access to the user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.98,
          "end": 261.08,
          "en": "and we're setting our LastName equal to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.08,
          "end": 265.13,
          "en": "And therefore, with all of that if we save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.13,
          "end": 269.69,
          "en": "I can enter max here, my watcher fires and I see max here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.69,
          "end": 271.7,
          "en": "But if I type here in the LastName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.7,
          "end": 273.58,
          "en": "this does not update automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.58,
          "end": 276.08,
          "en": "because we removed two way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.08,
          "end": 280.57,
          "en": "Instead, I can now click setLastName, and it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 280.57,
          "end": 282.823,
          "en": "And it also of course, triggers the watcher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 284.5,
          "end": 287.08299999999997,
          "en": "So that's how we can work with template refs.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
